  "summary": "Malicious code in chalk-lib (npm)",
  "details": "The postinstall hook of chalk-lib@1.0.0 (scripts/postinstall.js) is a dropper. It XOR-decodes an obfuscated URL and downloads a Windows executable (main.exe) from github[.]com/bebriz1/qPzM50V1aKG0rVlH/release/download/nqll/main.exe into %TEMP%, then executes it detached. On WSL/virtualized-Linux hosts it runs the same download-and-execute via a shell bridge command. It also POSTs host platform telemetry to 193[.]70[.]34[.]101:20099/vote. All network destinations are XOR-obfuscated in the script.",
